This file is never woven.  It holds one small program per test case of
the class files' [[tests]] programs in contents.nw, so that the deck can
show, beside each test case, what those lines print (didactic's
[[\runpython]]).  The test lines themselves are written once, as named
chunks in contents.nw; the programs here only reference them, and the
Makefile tangles them with both files (notangle concatenates the chunk
definitions of all its input files).

Each program imports the class, runs the earlier test cases of the same
[[tests]] with their output thrown away, and then runs the test case
it is named after.  The earlier cases set up the objects the case uses,
in the state [[tests]] leaves them in at that point, so the shown output
is exactly the lines [[tests]] prints for that case.

The programs live here and not in contents.nw because a root woven
there would either print eight harness chunks in the notes, or, hidden,
leave the test chunks' \enquote{used in} references pointing at labels
that do not exist.

